# Commercial web readiness

When editing lead forms, CRM/email delivery, homepage/nav IA, case studies,
About/leadership, CTAs, local SEO/LocalBusiness, health endpoints, client
portals, or conversion analytics, read and follow:

`.cursor/skills/commercial-web-readiness/SKILL.md`

(Also see `.cursor/skills/web-quality-standards/SKILL.md` for LCP, a11y, contrast, Zaraz, Co Spanish.)

**Keep the skill current:** when fixing a new commercial/credibility finding, update that skill (and this short list if non-negotiable) in the same PR.

Non-negotiables (details in the skill):

- Production lead endpoints never return `{ ok: true }` on console-only delivery — require Attio and/or Web3Forms (or equivalent durable sink); Attio failure must try the fallback before failing the user.
- Turnstile is required in production for public forms; missing secret fails closed.
- Founder-career results are never labeled as company “customers” without documentation — use explicit founder-leadership attribution.
- Homepage first impression states the primary recurring offer (for Cybercon: managed IT + cybersecurity); secondary projects stay nested.
- CTA copy must match what the page delivers (no fake instant cost calculator).
- Mailing/PMB addresses are labeled no customer visits; `areaServed` is the real service area.
- Public `/api/health` is `{ ok, time }` only; detail is authenticated.
- Protected `/client` (or equivalent) fails closed when auth is unconfigured.
- Prefer the skill’s priority order: revenue → credibility → positioning → proof → funnel → traffic.
